{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531865-storyteller-vault-book-idea-book-of-spheres-the-disparate-the-mad","id":1531865,"title":"Storyteller Vault Book Idea: Book of Spheres: The Disparate & The Mad","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-02T23:04:30-08:00","id":1531865,"title":"Storyteller Vault Book Idea: Book of Spheres: The Disparate & The Mad","content":"Hi y'all. So I haven't posted here in nearly 10 years! How have you been?<br /> <br /> So anyway I had this idea for a Storyteller's Vault book rattling around in my head for a few weeks and I thought I give an outline of it here to kind of workshop it.<br /> <br /> <b>Book of Spheres: The Disparate &amp; The Mad</b><br /> <br /> The basic idea is there are three Technocracy focused variant spheres already, so this book would explore variant spheres for the other six: three spheres utilized by different crafts, and three spheres for different mad/fallen mages. My current working ideas are:<br /> <br /> <b>Disparate</b> <b>Spheres</b><br /> Forces -&gt; Atar: A specialty of the Taftani, it envisions forces not through a modern scientific but rather a product of the holy flames of Ormazd, resulting in some differences in the exact type forces one can weild.<br /> <br /> Mind -&gt; Soul: Used by faith oriented crafts and focuses more on a spiritual interpretation of the mind.<br /> <br /> Entropy -&gt; Telos: The alleged 10th sphere of the Ixoi/Ksirafai/Janissaries can really be viewed as variant of entropy, where the ultimate fate is not the heat death of the universe but rather apocalyptic judgement.<br /> <br /> <b>Mad Spheres</b><br /> Life -&gt; Undeath: I actually already made a thread about this way back when. Used by high morbidity mages, liches, and lost books about it possibly tucked away somewhere in a Tremere chantry. Functions like the life sphere, but something is very... off about the supposed living beings made or enhanced by it.<br /> <br /> Time -&gt; Multiverse: Basically the time sphere operating under multiverse logic. Utilized by some Marauders and potentially explains their penchant for finding long lost bygone creatures, as well as tendency to seemingly blink out of existence.<br /> <br /> Matter -&gt; Antimatter: Perhaps the most dangerous variant, allowing user to manipulate antimatter, though there is the slight problem of what happens when matter and antimatter meet... Only the Nephandic Exies are demented enough to explore this variant in any sizable number.<br /> <br /> Any thought on my ideas so far would be highly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","user":"Becksworth","date":". 03-03-2024, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T23:12:18-08:00","id":1531866,"title":"","content":"Honestly after writing it out Mind/Soul kind of feels like the weak link here, so suggestions in particular there would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T06:51:53-08:00","id":1531878,"title":"","content":"Soul seems pretty good as just a a different take on Mind, but you could check out how different religions have conceived of the soul(s) and use that to extrapolate some different effects that might not be possible under Mind. I know some religions envisioned some souls provided the animating spark, while other souls were the conscious and/or unconscious mind. I'd take a look at the \u0101tman from hinduism since that is a major religion with a billion believers, buddhism also uses the same term but has a different take and also different buddhist traditions can be pretty divergent. The ancient egyptian souls would be good since egyptian practices inform a lot of modern occult practices. A lot has been written in WoD about the hun and po from taoism already, but maybe worth skimming some of that. Shinto has the mitama where all spirits (human and animistic) have four parts. I'm less familiar with early christian thinking on the soul, but I know there was lots of hellenistic influence on early christianity so there might be some interesting ideas there that small crafts might preserve that the mainline Chorus has abandoned over time. Actually, on that front gnosticism probably preserves a lot of those ideas so maybe start there, and gnosticism is pretty rife for mystic practices.<br /> <br /> Undeath made me think that from a certain perspective, the body is just made of matter. It's not like chemical and electrical reactions aren't happening once something dies, death is more of a gradient between two arbitrary definitions imposed on the world. You could maybe spin that idea out further to a Marauder take on Matter that encompasses Life as well.<br /> <br /> That also got me thinking there might be meat for a Nephandic take on &quot;time is a flat circle.&quot; There is no choice, no free will, you're just a machine with the illusion of consciousness and that illusion thinks it makes choices. That feels more like a Nephanic Mind rote that creates philosophical zombies though, obliterating someone's consciousness and leaving a shell that acts like them but isn't self-aware.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:24:45-08:00","id":1531879,"title":"","content":"You might want to look at the <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/388362\" target=\"_blank\">Book of Fragments</a>, which provides a robust system for Minor Spheres. I could see a Soul Minor Sphere that draws heavily on Mind, Prime, and Spirit, with maybe a touch of Entropy as well. <br /> <br /> As well, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/458587\" target=\"_blank\">Paradigm Explored: Eris and Enigma</a> includes a write-up of Telos as a Minor Sphere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T16:42:12-08:00","id":1531933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531865-storyteller-vault-book-idea-book-of-spheres-the-disparate-the-mad?p=1531878#post1531878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soul seems pretty good as just a a different take on Mind, but you could check out how different religions have conceived of the soul(s) and use that to extrapolate some different effects that might not be possible under Mind. I know some religions envisioned some souls provided the animating spark, while other souls were the conscious and/or unconscious mind. I'd take a look at the \u0101tman from hinduism since that is a major religion with a billion believers, buddhism also uses the same term but has a different take and also different buddhist traditions can be pretty divergent. The ancient egyptian souls would be good since egyptian practices inform a lot of modern occult practices. A lot has been written in WoD about the hun and po from taoism already, but maybe worth skimming some of that. Shinto has the mitama where all spirits (human and animistic) have four parts. I'm less familiar with early christian thinking on the soul, but I know there was lots of hellenistic influence on early christianity so there might be some interesting ideas there that small crafts might preserve that the mainline Chorus has abandoned over time. Actually, on that front gnosticism probably preserves a lot of those ideas so maybe start there, and gnosticism is pretty rife for mystic practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think the problem isn't necessarily soul is a bad idea for a variant so much as it could use more fleshing out/linking to a specific paradigm or concept to add more flavor to it. Another thing to think about is which crafts specialize in mind, which brings me to the Batini, except my other craft variants are middle easterm/middle east adjacent already...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T19:04:17-08:00","id":1531941,"title":"","content":"So looking at crafts specializing in mind I saw:<br /> <br /> Ahl i Batin<br /> Ngoma<br /> Sisters of Hippolyta<br /> Templar Knights<br /> <br /> Would like to avoid the Batini and the Sisters for the reason I mentioned above, and Templar Knight were kind of what I was thinking of with Soul and now kind of not feeling anymore.<br /> <br /> That leaves Ngoma, which actually gave me an idea.<br /> <br /> Mind -&gt; Knowledge, an Ngoma variant of mind that focuses on the concept of learning over the mind housing it.<br /> <br /> I would have to define what is knowledge vs parts of the human mind that aren't, as Knowledge the variant sphere wouldn't have dominion over those parts of your brain, but would also be able to derive knowledge from other sources (example: reading a book purely through holding it/osmosis).<br /> <br /> I'm liking that idea so far. Got more flavor to it, and it fits with the Ngoma (or what I've read of them at least). Any thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","user":"Becksworth","date":". 03-03-2024, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T07:35:21-07:00","id":1532325,"title":"","content":"I just fully customize my &quot;Spheres&quot;, to the point that they don't even &quot;exist&quot; at all in a sense. For I deal with each group having their own &quot;Realms&quot;. For instance, my Techies have &quot;Biochemistry&quot; and &quot;Space/Time&quot; rather than Life, Matter, Corr and Time. My Dreamspeakers have only 3 Realms, Body, Mind and Soul (and here the names are a bit misleading; the &quot;Mind&quot; realm deals with the &quot;world of the senses&quot;, so roughly speaking it would embark the &quot;traditional spheres&quot; of Time, Corr and Entropy, while &quot;Soul&quot; embarks Mind, Spirit and Prime, or that which creates the &quot;illusion of the self&quot;. Body, obviously, deals with the &quot;illusions&quot; of the Material World, therefore it is roughly Life, Matter and Forces). The OoH still have the &quot;vanilla&quot; 9 Spheres, but pretty much that only applies to them.<br /> <br /> This makes MagiK a LOT less communicable between different magical visions, and a lot more unique.<br /> <br /> I also use a lot of Minor &quot;Spheres&quot;. In my games, you'll hardly ever find a &quot;Forces Sphere Generalist&quot; Hermetic; most of the time, what you can expect is to find a &quot;Pyromancer&quot; (Minor Fire Sphere) or a &quot;Cryomancer&quot; (Minor &quot;Cryomancy&quot; - Ice - Sphere) or a &quot;Telekinesist&quot; (Minor &quot;Telekinesis&quot; - Movement - Sphere) and some such.<br /> <br /> So, the Mages on my tables will probably be an &quot;Cryomancer, Empath (Minor &quot;Empathy&quot; Sphere, aka the ability to manipulate emotions), &quot;Seer&quot; (Minor &quot;Divination&quot; Sphere, aka the ability to see into the past/future) and &quot;Chlorokinetic&quot; (Minor &quot;Chlorokinesis&quot; Sphere - aka the ability to manipulate plants) rather than generalist Forces, Mind, Time and Life users, so such a Mage is way more restricted in the areas they can act, but can pack a bigger punch in those niche areas.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T09:04:09-07:00","id":1532378,"title":"","content":"To give a status update as to where I'm at on this, I've actually made some good progress on a rough manuscript. I'm about 4 and 1/2 way through doing the rough write-ups for variant spheres and got an outline for the book. <br /> <br /> My rough idea is to start with a chapter broadly discussing variant sphere and how the Traditions, Technocracy, and Crafts broadly view things. Then a chapter with some Craft write ups based on groups that likely aren't going to get 20th Anniversary edition write ups at this point and made a good fit for various variant spheres. The 3rd chapter being the write ups for the craft variant spheres and some example rotes. The 4th chapter being the same for the same for the mad/fallen variants. Finally an appendix for any additional odds &amp; ends like merits &amp; flaws and wonders.<br /> <br /> Some ideas for crafts I like to include:<br /> The Ixoi - I mean Telos was one of the variants I settled on...<br /> Miarainohmen - Wouldn't use any of the variants I came up with, but would be a good example of mixing technocratic variant spheres on end and mystical practices on the other end.<br /> Red Thorn Dedicants - Their connection to Lilith/Bahari would make them a good fit for Undeath.<br /> The Hui:xa - The &quot;aliens&quot; that the Thal'un/Star Council were reseaching. They could use Multiverse, and I got the idea of making it nebulous on whether they are truly extraterrestrials, or possibly humans from an alternate earth.<br /> <br /> I would be interested in hearing people's thoughts on those. <br /> <br /> Also as an aside, I had the idea of &quot;fringe walker&quot; being an old tradition term used to describe crafts that utilized magick that didn't neatly fit into their sphere model, just as a nod to earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-15T19:38:02-07:00","id":1532678,"title":"","content":"So for the Red Thorn Dedicants, is there any material anywhere in Mage, Vampire, or just cWoD in general that goes into non vampire Lilith devotees? I have a rough idea for the craft, just didn't want to contradict some obscure bit of existing lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-23T10:50:00-07:00","id":1533040,"title":"","content":"Not sure if anyone is interested in status updates, but I got the variant spheres fleshed out and six craft write ups as well. Currently I'm writing a chapter one that goes over different teaching models of magicks (like self taught orphans -&gt; foundation/pillars -&gt; the Nine Spheres -&gt; the Nine Spheres plus Variants -&gt; grand unifying theories/Tenth Sphere), then do Rotes, an Appendix with odds and ends, and closing thoughts. Once that's all done I'll still have to do layout and picking out images to use. I'm thinking this will be around 60 pages when all said and done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-07T19:58:18-07:00","id":1533787,"title":"","content":"Status Update: Rough manuscript finished and starting the whole &quot;make this a pdf book&quot; process. My 60 page estimate was wrong, it's actually probably going to be around 100, so I managed to make a proper supplement here.<br /> <br /> Given the lack of feedback I'm kind of worried the project will just fade into obscurity if I overprice it, so I was kind of thinking perhaps going the &quot;pay what you want option&quot;. Any thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-15T21:07:45-07:00","id":1534287,"title":"","content":"Red-lining my rough draft is slow going, but got a 3rd of it done so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-03T07:07:17-07:00","id":1535103,"title":"","content":"Not sure if anyone here is knowledgeable on the what's in what art pack, but do they include the Telos/Tenth Sphere symbol in any of them? I know it's just an alchemy notation symbol for sulfur that just happened to look like a chair (ie the tenth seat), but I didn't want to pull it from elsewhere and end up getting in trouble because I wasn't permitted to use White Wolf's take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-01T19:33:27-07:00","id":1537977,"title":"","content":"So status update. After four months of work I uploaded it to the Storyteller's Vault. Final page count is around 100.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486515/The-Book-of-Spheres-Magicks-Disparate--Mad\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/pro...Disparate--Mad</a><br /> <br /> Would appreciate if knowing if anyone spots any typos we missed.<br /> <br /> Hope you all enjoy it.<a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486515/The-Book-of-Spheres-Magicks-Disparate--Mad\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</a>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T17:01:18-07:00","id":1544363,"title":"","content":"Just thought I'd share here, I was doing a 50% off sale for Halloween. Use the link below. Offer is valid until the end of October.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?discount=94f7e16198\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....unt=94f7e16198</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}